    "title": "What Notre Dame coach Niele Ivey said about UConn",
    "text": "FORT WORTH, TEXAS - MARCH 29: Head coach Geno Auriemma of UConn Huskies talks to head coach Niele Ivey of Notre Dame Fighting Irish before the game in the Elite Eight round game of the 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament held at Dickies Arena on March 29, 2026 in Fort Worth, Texas. (Photo by Andy Hancock/NCAA Photos/NCAA Photos via Getty Images)Andy Hancock/NCAA Photos/NCAA Photos via Getty ImagesThe UConn women's basketball team defeated Notre Dame 70-52 in the Elite Eight on Sunday.Notre Dame, and specifically its head coach Niele Ivey has been the program that has found the most success against UConn in recent decades.Article continues below this adEntering Sunday's NCAA tournament game, Notre Dame and UConn had met eight times in the NCAA Tournament, and Notre Dame had won five of those meetings. Ivey has a winning record against the Huskies both as a player and a coach during March Madness, but the Huskies emerged victorious this time. During a postgame press conference Ivey was asked about the Huskies, specifically if they have improved since the teams met during the regular season and what she thinks UConn will do in the Final Four. \"Blanca (Quiñonez) is something that didn't happen the first time around. She had a great game, and I'm sure she's going to feed off that energy in the Final Four,\" Ivey said in the press conference. \"Having everybody step up and being ready. I think they're just as solid. They're deep, and anybody can step up if others are not playing well. I mean, their two best players still ended with double figures. There's a very physical, very confident team. They play well with each other. Very disciplined. You know, they're a really, really good team.\"Article continues below this adFreshman Blanca Quiñonez helped lead UConn with 20 points and eight rebounds in the Elite Eight victory. Sarah Strong had a team-high 21 points to go along with seven rebounds and five steals.Azzi Fudd scored 13 points for UConn with four assists and three steals. Article continues below this adGet daily updates from the UConn basketball world.",
